  "biome_based_crops.guide.setup_text": "A sealed room registers as a biome when its required climate, native floor, and interior materials match; its natural mobs can then spawn there. Greenhouse growth outside direct thermoregulator coverage needs sky-exposed glass directly above each plant; the rest of the roof may be solid. A naturally matching room needs no AC. Otherwise, point an AC into the room and use one AC per 256 enclosed interior blocks. Separately, an active Electrical or Tough As Nails thermoregulator can support climate-based plants in a four-block front half-circle, one block above or below, without a greenhouse or overhead glass. Power or fuel and clear airflow are required; explicit biome rules still apply. On Sable ships, crops follow the biome at their current world location and local controllers move with them. Faint air wisps show leaks; seal them within one minute before the room climate returns toward its natural state.",
